{"nodes": [{"id": "design_prototype_notes_method", "label": "Prototype-Matching Notes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_token_snap_rule", "label": "Token Snap Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Snap to the nearest token when one exists, use an arbitrary value only when none can serve, and flag it. The prototypes use more sizes than the four the token file defines."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_cap_height_recovery", "label": "Cap-Height Font-Size Recovery", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "font-size ~= capHeight / 0.727 for Inter. Ink runs vary with which glyphs a line contains; the cap height of one flat-topped letter (T, F, H, M) is stable."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_cap_top_margin_formula", "label": "Cap-Top to CSS Margin Formula", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "capTop = boxTop + (lineHeight - 1.21*fontSize)/2 + 0.242*fontSize. Predicted every About margin to within ~10px on the first try."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_screenshot_stitching", "label": "Screenshot Stitching Method", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Brute-force row-match each overlapping capture pair over the FULL range; a truncated search window silently locks onto a bogus match in a blank region. Reject err-0 matches whose band is uniform."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_absent_content_trap", "label": "Do Not Infer Absent Content From a Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On About, a plausible bottom padding closed the gap after the chiefs - two whole staff rows were hiding in there. Ask for the missing screenshot instead."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_image_cache_volatility", "label": "Image Cache Holds Only the Latest Message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "~/.claude/image-cache/<session-id>/ is renumbered each time, so measure every batch the moment it lands. Eyeballing a render is good to about +/-10px, not enough for margin work."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_ratio_crops", "label": "Express Crops as Viewport-Width Ratios", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client's browser is ~1849px wide and test viewports are 1440, so absolute px crops do not transfer. aspect-[w/h] + object-cover + a percentage object-position is scale-invariant."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale", "label": "portal-scale Zoom Utility", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The portal is measured in literal px off a 1440x810 frame, so on a wider window it holds absolute size and shrinks proportionally. portal-scale zooms it by clamp(1, tan(atan2(100vw,1440px)) * 0.9, 2). The @property registration is load-bearing: it computes on :root where zoom is still 1, instead of feeding back on itself."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale_damping", "label": "The *0.9 Damping Is Deliberate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A strict frame-width scale read a touch large to the owner (2026-07-23), so it is damped 10%. It is the tuning knob. Side effect: nothing scales until ~1600 wide, since below that the damped ratio is under the floor of 1."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_zoom_viewport_units_trap", "label": "zoom Does Not Rescale Viewport Units", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A plain h-screen on the zoomed element lays out scale-times too tall (360px of overflow at 1920) and steals scrolling from main. The utility owns height: calc(100dvh / var(--portal-scale)) for exactly that reason."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_text_title_leading_trap", "label": "text-title 1.5 Line-Height Trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tailwind v4 gives text-title a 1.5 line-height (54px) where the prototypes use ~1.2. Every heading needs explicit leading-[1.2] or the page drifts ~11px per heading - the biggest single source of vertical error on About."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_next_image_true_size", "label": "Next <Image> True Pixel Size Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "width/height must be the file's TRUE pixel size or artifacts bake into the cached WebP. After changing a file in public/, rm -rf .next/dev/cache/images."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_jsx_space_eating", "label": "JSX Silently Eats Spaces Around </strong>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guard with a DOM assertion comparing textContent to the expected string; putting copy in string arrays sidesteps it entirely."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_ink_overflow_scan", "label": "Ink Overflow Needs scrollWidth, Not getBoundingClientRect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_lazy_image_screenshot", "label": "Lazy Images Are Blank in a fullPage Screenshot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scroll first, then waitForFunction over document.images checking complete && naturalWidth > 0."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_dev_indicator_corruption", "label": "Next Dev Indicator Corrupts Pixel Scans", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_about_page_facts", "label": "About Page Match Facts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "max-w-[1152px] container, hero cropped to the prototype band ratio, the only justified text on the site, employee PNGs ship with a 5px frame baked into the file, and the prototype's oversized PALMA/DISTOR names were normalised on purpose."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_accreditations_page_facts", "label": "Accreditations Page Match Facts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:109", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hero aspect-[3.66] object-[center_38%] is settled - a tighter crop was tried and rejected. Stat cards 168x168, 61px gap, numeral gold keyline is four 1px offset text-shadows."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_gov_recognitions_page_facts", "label": "Gov. Recognitions Page Match Facts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:115", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Content is placeholder matching the prototype; the RECOGNITIONS array is the swap point. The hero is soft in the source asset - needs a client re-export >=1850px, not a quality flag."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_campuses_page_facts", "label": "Campuses Page Match Facts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:123", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Route is /about/campuses. The card grid is flex-wrap + justify-center, not grid, which is what centres the lone 22nd card that grid-cols-3 would left-align."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_campuses_stat_band_scale_up", "label": "Campuses Stat Band Scaled Up on Request", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:141", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client asked for the band bigger than the prototype (2026-07-22), so it is deliberately off-prototype. The 365px side rules could not survive the scale-up and are now flex-1; do not restore w-[365px] without shrinking the type back."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_dropdown_spec", "label": "About Dropdown Measured Spec", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:169", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Matched to within 1px. bg-gray/15 over white computes to exactly #EBEBEB, the measured fill, so no arbitrary hex was needed. The prototype shows no active-page styling on dropdown items, so that distinction was deliberately removed rather than overlooked."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_hover_feedback", "label": "Client Rejected the Hover Pill", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:163", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hover must darken the font only, no container background. The active link keeps its solid maroon pill - that is the current-page indicator, not hover."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_height_mismatch", "label": "Navbar Height Mismatch: 58px vs 80px", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The prototype navbar is ~58px tall against our 80px and its wordmark is all-caps. Not reconciled, and touching it moves every page."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_missing_employee_assets", "label": "Missing Employee Portrait Assets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:180", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PALMA, ENTIENZA, DISTOR and TRANCE were lifted 1:1 from client screenshots and re-framed; swap when real exports arrive."}, {"id": "design_prototype_notes_prototype_slips", "label": "Prototype Content Slips Reproduced Faithfully", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:184", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two reds on the campuses stat band (#990000 vs the #800000 token), ALFONSO and CABIAO both citing RA 11754, and inconsistent statute emphasis were reproduced rather than normalised, and flagged to the client instead."}], "edges": [{"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_token_snap_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_cap_height_recovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_cap_top_margin_formula", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_screenshot_stitching", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_absent_content_trap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_image_cache_volatility", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_ratio_crops", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_text_title_leading_trap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_next_image_true_size", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_jsx_space_eating", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_lazy_image_screenshot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_dev_indicator_corruption", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_ink_overflow_scan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_about_page_facts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_accreditations_page_facts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_gov_recognitions_page_facts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_campuses_page_facts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_method", "target": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_dropdown_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_cap_height_recovery", "target": "design_prototype_notes_cap_top_margin_formula", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:26", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale", "target": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale_damping", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:61", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_portal_scale", "target": "design_prototype_notes_zoom_viewport_units_trap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:52", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_token_snap_rule", "target": "design_figma_tokens_source_of_truth", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:8", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_campuses_page_facts", "target": "design_prototype_notes_campuses_stat_band_scale_up", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/prototype-notes.md", "source_location": "design/prototype-notes.md:141", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_dropdown_spec", "target": "design_prototype_notes_navbar_hover_feedback", "relation": "references", "co